WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.838
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim,

00:00:02.838 --> 00:00:04.650
and this is Geshe Michael Roach.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.750
We're ready now to start the actual

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.970
back into the Lam Rim text.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:15.342
What's exciting is that we have reached

00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:16.428
NYIN BCU BDUN PAR

00:00:16.428 --> 00:00:18.860
NYIN BCU BDUN PAR

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.553
It means, this is an
announcement in the text,

00:00:22.553 --> 00:00:27.553
that we have reached the
17th day of teaching.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.750
So, don't forget that this entire book

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.092
was a twenty four day teaching

00:00:34.092 --> 00:00:36.270
by the great Pabongka Rinpoche,

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.777
who was also a teacher
of my teacher's teacher,

00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:43.093
and one of the greatest books
ever written in Tibetan,

00:00:43.093 --> 00:00:45.100
maybe the greatest.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.960
NYIN BCU BDUN PAR means

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.880
we're starting on the record

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.520
of the 17th day of teachings.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.372
That makes us about 80% finished.

00:00:58.372 --> 00:01:03.372
We started this book I
guess over 10 years ago,

00:01:03.485 --> 00:01:07.510
and personally I'm just enjoying the book.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.500
I'm not trying to get through it

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.960
and try to finish it by certain date.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.160
I'm not thinking like that.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.570
I'm trying to, personally,

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:20.260
I'm trying to enjoy it
and go through it very...

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:23.290
with a lot of pleasure and enjoyment.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.510
I don't know, maybe like
people drink a fine wine.

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:26.970
I don't know, but just,

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.232
you don't rush to finish the bottle.

00:01:29.232 --> 00:01:32.260
You just sit and enjoy it.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.210
So we're enjoying the Lam Rim together.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.240
And, personally, I don't
care how long it takes.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.840
I think we should do it very deeply.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.790
In this course, we are
going to do it deeply.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:46.752
So we're about 80% finished.

00:01:46.752 --> 00:01:50.619
There's twenty four days
total. But don't forget,

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:53.880
we finished two of those
days already towards the end.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.880
And that's the teaching on
meditation and wisdom, emptiness.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.310
We did those at the
beginning of this 10 years

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.940
because we wanted to use the meditations

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.020
during the Lam Rim classes.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.580
So we've actually finished
about 80% of the text.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:16.060
I guess we can finish in
about four or five more years.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.820
Then I made you a promise for dessert.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.723
We're going to go to the great,

00:02:22.723 --> 00:02:26.047
greatest Lam Rim emptiness
teaching of ever.

00:02:26.047 --> 00:02:29.370
The emptiness teaching in this Lam Rim,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.750
called the Gift of Liberation

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.060
Thrust into the Palm of Your Hand.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:40.060
The presentation of emptiness
is actually not that long.

00:02:40.068 --> 00:02:45.068
The reason is that
Tsongkapa did it so well

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.000
and so long with Manjushri's help.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.040
I think Pabongka Rinpoche was thinking,

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.376
Oh, we don't have to,

00:02:51.376 --> 00:02:53.470
we don't have to cover it that much here.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.610
So we're going to go, after
we finished this Lam Rim,

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.830
we're going to go study
the emptiness chapter

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.020
in the meditation chapter

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:05.900
from Tsongkapa's great book
on the Steps of the Path,

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.690
which is LAM RIM CHEN MO

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:11.119
That will take us about
six years, so don't worry.

00:03:11.119 --> 00:03:14.370
We have only about ten years left to go.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:18.920
Don't gobble down this fine wine.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.208
Enjoy it. Have fun.

00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:24.320
It's a way of life.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.640
Lam Rim is not a book.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.510
Lam Rim is a way of life
for the rest of your life.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:32.543
If you can get Lam Rim teachings

00:03:32.543 --> 00:03:35.310
for most of your adult life, which I did,

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.840
you'll be very grateful.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.830
It keeps your life going straight,

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.360
through all the changes
that we have in our life.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:47.400
The Lam Rim can be the one steady thing

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.450
that you keep doing
through your whole life.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.713
Here we go.

00:03:51.713 --> 00:03:52.979
NYIN BCU BDUN PAR

00:03:52.979 --> 00:03:55.180
RGYAL SRAS CHEN PO ZHI BA LHA'I ZHAL NAS

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:59.680
means let's talk, I'd like
to give you a quotation

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.965
from that great bodhisattva

00:04:01.965 --> 00:04:04.248
RGYAL SRAS CHEN PO ZHI BA LHA

00:04:04.248 --> 00:04:05.489
Shantideva

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:07.514
Here's the quotation:

00:04:07.514 --> 00:04:10.639
,GANG LA SEMS KYI DAM PA RIN CHEN DE,

00:04:10.639 --> 00:04:13.138
,SKYES PA DE YI SKU LA PHYAG 'TSAL ZHING,

00:04:13.138 --> 00:04:16.355
,GANG LA GNOD PA BYAS KYANG BDE 'BREL BA,

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:18.663
,BDE BA'I 'BYUNG GNAS
DE LA SKYABS SU MCHI,

00:04:18.663 --> 00:04:20.040
I bow down

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.000
to that precious state of mind,

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.060
to the jewel of that state of mind.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.933
Well what state of mind are
you talking about Shantideva?

00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:31.450
He says, Well, there's a state of mind

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:36.450
that if you have it and
someone bows down to you,

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.210
they make incredible good karma.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.490
We talked about it in the coffee shop.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:45.040
If you're a secret
bodhisattva, which you can be,

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.360
and you're sitting in the coffee shop,

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.540
and somebody offers you a coffee,

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.980
they get like a billion
years of good karma.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.260
It's so cool.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:57.590
It's so sexy to be the
person who can quietly

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:00.697
make other people a billion
years of good karma,

00:05:00.697 --> 00:05:03.360
just by buying a coffee from them.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.330
But obviously, if they
make a prostration to you,

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.260
they will get intense good karma.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:12.686
Now comes controversial part.

00:05:12.686 --> 00:05:16.100
GANG LA GNOD PA BYAS KYANG BDE 'BREL BA

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.210
Wouldn't it be cool to
be the kind of person

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:23.017
that if someone hurt you,
they would make good karma?

00:05:23.017 --> 00:05:26.330
What?

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.705
If someone hurt you, they
would make good karma.

00:05:29.705 --> 00:05:33.340
Come on, Geshe-la, we know many examples.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:36.000
If you do bad thing to bodhisattva,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.370
you get bad karma for a long, long time.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:41.070
Yes. But something happens cool.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.610
Even if you hurt a bodhisattva,

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.051
you get BDE 'BREL

00:05:44.051 --> 00:05:45.630
BDE 'BREL means

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.090
you make a karmic connection
with them, you see.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:50.996
Even if you yell at a bodhisattva

00:05:50.996 --> 00:05:54.130
or you say something bad
about this bodhisattva,

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:56.080
then, of course you make a bad seed.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:00.390
But you also make a connection
seed with the bodhisattva.

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:01.740
It's very interesting.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.823
That will bring you happiness
for millions of lifetimes.

00:06:05.823 --> 00:06:07.140
It's so cool.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:10.260
So if I can become bodhisattva,

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.876
if I can have bodhisattva's vision,

00:06:13.876 --> 00:06:16.700
then of course, if someone
serves me a coffee,

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:19.380
secretly, I will give them a
billion years of good karma.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:20.890
That's sweet.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:24.074
Oh and even if they yell at
me or they call me stupid,

00:06:24.074 --> 00:06:25.970
"Geshe Michael, you're stupid."

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.680
Then of course, they
will make some bad karma

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:32.820
but they will make this
karma of connection

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.180
with a bodhisattva.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:36.610
And that karma is much more powerful.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.870
They will have this very
sweet karma of connection

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:40.703
with the bodhisattva.

00:06:40.703 --> 00:06:45.703
So Shantideva is bowing
down to bodhichitta

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.140
because of it's beautiful qualities.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.140
It's like a jewel.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.313
It's like a wish-giving jewel.

00:06:51.313 --> 00:06:53.812
GANG ZHIG RGYUD LA SKYES PA DE LA

00:06:53.812 --> 00:06:55.087
SKUR BA 'DEBS PA SOGS NGAN PA'I

00:06:55.087 --> 00:06:57.279
'BREL BA BZHAG PA TSUN KYANG

00:06:57.279 --> 00:06:59.420
Even if you do the worst thing possible

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:03.030
to bodhisattva, and you
criticize them. and spit on them,

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:07.017
or you something, you say
bad things about them.

00:07:07.017 --> 00:07:10.057
TSUN KYANG even up to,

00:07:10.057 --> 00:07:14.140
GTAN GYI BDE BAR 'GOD PAR
MDZAD PA'I PHAN YON CAN

00:07:15.406 --> 00:07:20.151
That bodhichitta can
still give you Buddhahood.

00:07:20.151 --> 00:07:24.390
Even from making a bad
connection with a bodhisattva,

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:27.470
because you made a connection
with a bodhisattva,

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:30.390
that bodhichitta is so powerful

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:33.110
that somehow it's going
to take those other people

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.300
to enlightenment when they criticize you.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.273
So that's kind of cool, right?

00:07:37.273 --> 00:07:41.020
BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS KYI PHAN
YON 'GA' ZHIG GSUNGS NAS

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:43.330
This GSUNGS NAS means - our Lama

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.000
started out the seventeenth day

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.310
by reminding us of how
cool is bodhichitta.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.993
GSUNGS means he reminded us.

00:07:51.993 --> 00:07:55.450
PHAN YON 'GA' ZHIG means
he threw in a couple

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.590
of more benefits about bodhichitta

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:00.250
that he did not mention
in the previous day.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:01.930
He added some more.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:04.720
That what's the new benefit we have?

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.530
Insult a bodhisattva

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.910
and you make a connection
to become a Buddha.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:11.507
Yay!

00:08:11.507 --> 00:08:16.329
MDOR NA SEMS 'DIS ZIN
PA'I BYAS TSAD CHOS DANG

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:20.570
There's a very important
word here called ZIN PA

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:23.050
Z-I-N-P-A.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:24.970
ZIN PA

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.420
Very, very important word.

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:30.520
It's very difficult to
translate into English

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:35.160
but it means, I don't know,
when you're in high school

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.390
and your hormones are flowing strong,

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:41.790
which in some men don't
finish until you're 85 or 90.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.987
I don't know.

00:08:42.987 --> 00:08:46.220
But you fall in love
with every girl you see

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:47.450
on the street.

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:51.610
We were talking about Don Juan, right?

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.260
No, Don Quixote.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.682
Sorry.

00:08:54.682 --> 00:08:58.732
That he fall in love with this bar girl.

00:08:58.732 --> 00:09:02.210
What's her name?

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:05.330
I forgot.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.163
I forgot her name.

00:09:06.163 --> 00:09:09.443
Anyway, if the young man fall in love

00:09:09.443 --> 00:09:11.290
with this girl in high school,

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:13.731
then all the time he's thinking
about her, all the time.

00:09:13.731 --> 00:09:16.540
He's driving, he's thinking about...

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.730
Everything reminds him

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:21.440
of this new girl he met in the high school

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:22.970
and that's called ZIN PA

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:24.930
In Tibetan that's called ZIN PA

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:29.930
His mind is captured by
these feelings for the girl.

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:31.991
In the bodhisattva's mind,

00:09:31.991 --> 00:09:36.560
ZIN PA captured by this
feeling that I would like

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:39.027
to become a Buddha for everybody.

00:09:39.027 --> 00:09:39.860
ZIN PA

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.126
That's ZIN PA

00:09:41.126 --> 00:09:44.699
MDOR NA SEMS 'DIS ZIN PA'I BYAS TSAD CHOS

00:09:44.699 --> 00:09:49.683
means once you have
bodhichitta stuck in your mind,

00:09:51.403 --> 00:09:55.503
like that cute girl's
picture in your mind,

00:09:55.503 --> 00:09:56.919
from that time,

00:09:56.919 --> 00:09:58.619
DE'ANG SANGS RGYAS KYI
RGYU THEG CHEN GYI CHOS

00:09:58.619 --> 00:09:59.460
SU 'GRO BA YIN PA'I PHYIR

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:04.242
Then anything you do becomes a cause

00:10:04.242 --> 00:10:05.510
for your enlightenment.

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:08.970
Once you are thinking about this girl,

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:11.440
meaning this Buddhahood,

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:14.010
then it doesn't matter what you do.

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.640
That becomes a cause for Buddhahood.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:19.132
And we have a picture here,

00:10:19.132 --> 00:10:22.637
it's a guy taking a walk with his dog

00:10:22.637 --> 00:10:24.730
or a lady taking a walk

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.078
with her husband and a dog.

00:10:27.078 --> 00:10:30.241
Just if a bodhisattva

00:10:30.241 --> 00:10:34.580
has got the bodhisattva
state of mind in their mind,

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:38.492
bodhisattva vision of
dancing between planets,

00:10:38.492 --> 00:10:41.357
if they have that in their mind,

00:10:41.357 --> 00:10:43.920
then everything they do is dharma.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.690
That's really cool.

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:48.510
Like you don't have to go to the temple

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:50.710
and read a Medicine Buddha Sutra.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:55.695
Go for a walk with your
dog and your husband,

00:10:55.695 --> 00:10:57.070
that's dharma.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:11:01.180
If you're thinking about
this vision that I would like

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.080
to dance between many
planets and help people.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.307
If you're thinking about that,

00:11:06.307 --> 00:11:07.532
then everything you do,

00:11:07.532 --> 00:11:09.070
you brush your teeth,

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:09.903
I don't know,

00:11:09.903 --> 00:11:11.480
you watch Netflix,

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.530
everything you do becomes dharma.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:14.640
It's very beautiful.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.750
It's very, very cool.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.043
Let's go to the next sentence.

00:11:19.043 --> 00:11:21.060
SGRUB PA NYAMS LEN BYED PA LA

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:21.893
Now he says

00:11:21.893 --> 00:11:24.721
let's put it in the context of practice.

00:11:24.721 --> 00:11:28.037
SGRUB PA NYAMS LEN means

00:11:28.037 --> 00:11:30.900
how does this bodhisattva's vision

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.854
going to affect your Buddhist practice?

00:11:32.854 --> 00:11:35.412
LHA BGSOM SNGAGS BZLAS TZAM
LAS BYED RGYU MED PA BZHIN

00:11:35.412 --> 00:11:36.245
MI BYED PAR

00:11:36.245 --> 00:11:38.178
Forget

00:11:38.178 --> 00:11:39.461
LHA BSGOM

00:11:39.461 --> 00:11:41.625
Forget meditating on Medicine Buddha.

00:11:41.625 --> 00:11:45.256
LHA BSGOM forget doing
Medicine Buddha's mantras.

00:11:45.256 --> 00:11:47.659
BYED RGYU MED PA BZYIN MI BYED PAR

00:11:47.659 --> 00:11:49.975
Even if you don't do anything

00:11:49.975 --> 00:11:50.808
SGRUP PA

00:11:50.808 --> 00:11:53.493
Don't think about those
high, high practices.

00:11:53.493 --> 00:11:56.419
SGRUB PA NYAMS SU BLANG BYA'I GZHI MA

00:11:56.419 --> 00:12:00.439
By the way, this MA,
Tim, is not a negative.

00:12:00.439 --> 00:12:03.970
It's the second half of GZHI

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:04.930
It's interesting.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:06.400
So you have to be careful.

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:09.680
It means that the super foundation,

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.044
like the mother foundation.

00:12:11.044 --> 00:12:12.285
GZHI MA

00:12:12.285 --> 00:12:13.759
BYANG CHUB LAM RIM DANG,

00:12:13.759 --> 00:12:14.834
DE'I NANG NAS KYANG BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS

00:12:14.834 --> 00:12:15.667
'DI LA BYED DGOS KYI

00:12:15.667 --> 00:12:20.660
He says, forget secret mantras.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:23.840
Forget a meditation on

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.320
even Medicine Buddha.

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:30.090
Right now, if you focus on this feeling

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:32.810
that I would like to
dance between the planets

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.040
and help other beings there,

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.240
you focus on that feeling,

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.600
and that's enough for your practice.

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:43.210
That's extremely powerful
Vajrayana practice

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:47.240
is to love other people
enough that you want to dance

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.240
between a billion planets and help them.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.560
Keep that vision in your mind,

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:55.670
and it's as powerful as tantra.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.010
Keep that vision in your mind.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:00.254
Then he says in the next sentence,

00:13:00.254 --> 00:13:04.144
'DI MED PA MI TSE RI STONG DU BSKYAL TE

00:13:04.144 --> 00:13:05.619
RI STONG

00:13:05.619 --> 00:13:07.182
RI means a mountain.

00:13:07.182 --> 00:13:09.567
Like when we do the mandala, we say

00:13:09.567 --> 00:13:11.030
RI'I RGYAL PO RI RAB

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.576
which means the mountain.

00:13:12.576 --> 00:13:13.901
Mount Мeru.

00:13:13.901 --> 00:13:15.990
STONG means empty. So,

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:17.956
RI STONG means you climb up

00:13:17.956 --> 00:13:19.456
to the Himalayan mountains,

00:13:19.456 --> 00:13:22.227
you find a cave and you start meditating.

00:13:22.227 --> 00:13:24.940
GZHAN JI 'DRA ZHIG BSGOM KHUL BYAS KYANG

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:26.900
Doesn't matter what you do.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:29.572
By the way, Tim, the KHUL is new for you,

00:13:29.572 --> 00:13:31.550
K-H-U-L

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:36.250
That means, act like
you're doing something.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:40.500
Like you go through the motions is KHUL

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.770
It doesn't mean cool.

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:45.735
So when you add it to a verb,

00:13:45.735 --> 00:13:48.735
it means, yeah yeah you
look like you're meditating.

00:13:48.735 --> 00:13:50.477
You look like you went up on a mountain

00:13:50.477 --> 00:13:52.360
and you're sitting in a cave,

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.950
and you look like you're meditating.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:54.783
You're going through all the motions

00:13:54.783 --> 00:13:56.541
BYAS KYANG But

00:13:56.541 --> 00:13:58.687
SANGS RGYAS KYI GO 'PHANG
DANG CUNG ZAD KYANG

00:13:58.687 --> 00:14:00.437
NYE RU MI 'GRO BAS

00:14:00.437 --> 00:14:03.535
If you don't have this
bodhisattva's vision,

00:14:03.535 --> 00:14:06.550
you can spend a whole lifetime

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.870
in a meditation cave in the Himalayas

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.178
and you will not get closer,

00:14:11.178 --> 00:14:12.021
NYE RU

00:14:12.021 --> 00:14:15.748
you will not get closer
to Buddhahood, at all.

00:14:15.748 --> 00:14:17.815
CUNG ZAD

00:14:17.815 --> 00:14:19.290
You will not get closer to Buddhahood

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.281
if you don't have this vision.

00:14:21.281 --> 00:14:24.546
'DI NYID THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL DU GNANG DGOS

00:14:24.546 --> 00:14:27.485
So this is an important
new word for everybody

00:14:27.485 --> 00:14:28.627
THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL

00:14:28.627 --> 00:14:33.484
Say: THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL

00:14:33.484 --> 00:14:35.459
THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL

00:14:35.459 --> 00:14:38.000
MTHIL means the palm of your hand

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:43.000
And it also means the sole of your foot.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.010
This is where you get your wheels

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:47.267
when you get the marks
of a Buddha, for example,

00:14:47.267 --> 00:14:49.425
on your MTHIL

00:14:49.425 --> 00:14:53.502
But in Tibetan, spoken Tibetan,

00:14:53.502 --> 00:14:56.449
when you say put it in
your palm of your hand,

00:14:56.449 --> 00:15:00.276
similar to the title of this book,

00:15:00.276 --> 00:15:03.000
it means keep that as your main practice.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:07.068
There's something... You
got a picture for me?

00:15:07.068 --> 00:15:12.068
Yes. Keep this feeling
in the palm of your hand.

00:15:13.269 --> 00:15:15.268
It means

00:15:15.268 --> 00:15:16.443
THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL

00:15:16.443 --> 00:15:18.384
THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL

00:15:18.384 --> 00:15:22.213
means keep that as your
number one practice.

00:15:22.213 --> 00:15:24.570
THUGS DAM It means in
the palm of your hand,

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:28.080
in Tibetan means, keep that vision

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:30.600
of you dancing between planets.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:33.680
Keep that as your main,
main, main practice.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:36.090
That's called the practice

00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:38.100
that's in the middle of
the palm of your hand.

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:42.543
It's something you carry
around all the time.

00:15:42.543 --> 00:15:44.102
DE LTA BU'I

00:15:44.102 --> 00:15:45.548
Let's go back to the Tibetan.

00:15:45.548 --> 00:15:49.148
DE LTA BU'I SEMS DE BSKYED PA LA'ANG,

00:15:49.148 --> 00:15:52.439
SEMS SBYONG GI MAN NGAG
LA LTOS DGOS TSUL SOGS

00:15:52.439 --> 00:15:55.377
This is the most beautiful
part of this Tibetan.

00:15:55.377 --> 00:16:00.370
I'm going to say that
about a hundred times.

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.850
If you just know the instructions,

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.010
you need the instruction manual
for how to get bodhichitta,

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.760
that's all, he says, that's all.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:13.755
Look, there's one page
list, stuff you have to do.

00:16:13.755 --> 00:16:16.250
Then you get bodhichitta.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:19.190
Just look, there's a very easy list.

00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:23.250
You just follow seven instructions

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.630
and you get there.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:26.280
So let's do it together, okay?

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:27.680
Just seven instructions.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:30.720
You don't have to meditate for 20 years.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.470
They're just seven
steps, seven easy steps.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.147
Just do them.

00:16:36.147 --> 00:16:37.916
And then you get it.

00:16:37.916 --> 00:16:40.450
MAN NGAG LA LTOS DGOS TSUL

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.280
means our Lama impressed on us.

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:46.980
Just do those. I'm going to
teach you some instructions

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:49.407
and you just follow them.

00:16:49.407 --> 00:16:54.323
KUN SLONG 'CHOS LUGS
MDOR BSDUR SHIG STZAL NAS

00:16:54.323 --> 00:16:56.860
Every time that you
start a dharma teaching,

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:59.260
you have to get your
students into the mood.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:01.370
You have to say, look,

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:04.210
the virus was nothing.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.230
Four million people,

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:09.290
three million people die, is nothing.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.340
Seven billion people
died, that's something.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.270
Eight billion people
died, that's something.

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:18.665
So don't forget. Why are we doing Lam Rim?

00:17:18.665 --> 00:17:23.140
The virus was nothing. Three
million people are nothing.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:26.670
Seven billion people going to
die if we don't do something.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.880
They're not going to die from the virus.

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:31.305
They're going to die from getting old

00:17:31.305 --> 00:17:33.179
and die.

00:17:33.179 --> 00:17:35.060
We already had a virus before the virus.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:37.750
It was called "living."

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:40.430
We're all going to die from it.

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:43.150
So he says, don't forget the motivation,

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:44.900
why we are here,

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:46.290
why we are studying Lam Rim.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:50.270
Don't forget that on the seventeenth day,

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.190
the teacher, Pabongka Rinpoche,

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:54.015
reminded us why we were here.

00:17:54.015 --> 00:17:56.027
So never forget.

00:17:56.027 --> 00:17:59.926
SNGON DU JI LTAR SONG BA'I
SA BCAD RNAMS GSUNGS RJES

00:17:59.926 --> 00:18:01.890
That RJES means afterwards.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:06.740
It means he went through the outline

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:08.390
that we covered in the last course,

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:09.560
which I just did with you,

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.559
the ten benefits of bodhichitta.

00:18:12.559 --> 00:18:17.559
BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS KYI
PHAN YON DANG BTANG SNYOMS

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:21.430
He reviewed the ten
benefits of this vision

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:22.263
of the bodhisattva,

00:18:22.263 --> 00:18:24.253
which we just did in the last class.

00:18:25.341 --> 00:18:28.070
BTANG SNYOMS BSGOM PA
LA BSKYAR BSHAD MDZAD

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:30.528
And he talked about,

00:18:30.528 --> 00:18:34.442
you're going to build this
seven steps to bodhichitta,

00:18:34.442 --> 00:18:37.165
you're going to build them on upeksha

00:18:37.165 --> 00:18:39.065
what's upeksha, Timothy?

00:18:41.125 --> 00:18:43.170
upeksha

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:44.110
Equanimity. Yess

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:47.650
So don't forget, you
got to have equanimity

00:18:47.650 --> 00:18:50.200
before you can build love on top of it.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.800
You have to treat people equally

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.858
before you can learn to love people.

00:18:54.858 --> 00:18:58.550
Before you can really
learn to love people,

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:01.230
you have to see people as equal.

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:03.330
So he explained it

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.355
BSKYAR BSHAD MDZAD

00:19:04.355 --> 00:19:07.530
means he repeated from the last class

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:09.790
and then we went on to the new class.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.627
So here's the new class.

00:19:11.627 --> 00:19:14.576
DE NAS BYANG CHUB SEMS
SBYONG GI MAN NGAG BDUN GYI

00:19:14.576 --> 00:19:16.300
DANG PO NI MAR SHES YIN LA

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:18.540
You guys, should learn the word MAR SHES

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.400
MAR SHES in the second line.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.410
First part of this second line.

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:25.149
MAR SHES

00:19:25.149 --> 00:19:28.240
Yhis is what we're
going to focus on today.

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:29.540
It's called MAR SHES

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:34.250
MAR SHES means realize,
they are your mother.

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:37.500
MAR SHES means realize,
they are your mother.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.440
This is the first step

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:43.140
to developing that bodhisattva's vision.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:45.700
You have to understand
they are your mother,

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:46.760
MAR SHES YIN LA

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:49.173
Then he says,

00:19:49.173 --> 00:19:50.573
'DI RGYUD LA SKYE SHIN TU DKA'

00:19:50.573 --> 00:19:52.395
'DI RGYUD LA SKYE SHIN TU DKA'

00:19:52.395 --> 00:19:56.551
It's extremely difficult to reach.

00:19:56.551 --> 00:19:58.492
'DI RGYUD LA SKYE SHIN TU DKA'

00:19:58.492 --> 00:20:00.010
This RGYUD means mind,

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:04.310
to develop this in your
mind, is extremely difficult.

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:09.310
To really believe that
the people around you

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:13.475
have been your mother
is extremely difficult.

00:20:13.475 --> 00:20:15.341
RGYUD LA SKYE DKA' ZHING,
MA SKYES NA DRIN DRAN

00:20:15.341 --> 00:20:18.590
SOGS RGYU 'BRAS PHYI
MA RNAMS MI 'BYUNG BAS

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:19.980
But if you don't get past through

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:22.510
this first step of the seven,

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:26.028
you can forget trying to be a bodhisattva.

00:20:26.028 --> 00:20:31.028
If you don't get to the
point where you realize

00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:36.000
that all the people around
you have been your mom before,

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.360
forget being a bodhisattva.

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:38.193
Not possible.

00:20:38.193 --> 00:20:40.418
So, okay,

00:20:40.418 --> 00:20:41.584
Pabongka Rinpoche says,

00:20:41.584 --> 00:20:42.917
Look, I know it's difficult,

00:20:42.917 --> 00:20:45.817
it's not easy, but we got to start there

00:20:45.817 --> 00:20:47.940
and you got to recognize

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:50.214
that everyone has been your mother.

00:20:50.214 --> 00:20:52.068
'DI LA NAN TAN 'BAD DGOS

00:20:52.068 --> 00:20:54.890
means so you got to
work hard on this, okay?

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:58.860
You got to focus at the beginning

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:03.110
on treating, seeing
people have been your mom,

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:03.943
that's all.

00:21:03.943 --> 00:21:06.820
You have to focus on
that at the beginning.

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:09.661
And then he says,

00:21:09.661 --> 00:21:11.919
DE LA RGYU DANG PO MAR SHES NI,

00:21:11.919 --> 00:21:13.455
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD GNYEN GYI MTHAR THUG

00:21:13.455 --> 00:21:14.780
GNYEN GYI MTHAR THUG

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:16.610
GNYEN means relation,

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:20.170
like relative in your family.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:22.580
GNYEN GYI MTHAR THUG
means ultimate relative,

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:24.617
which is your mom.

00:21:24.617 --> 00:21:27.125
MAR SHES STE, 'DI RGYUD LA MA SKYES NA

00:21:27.125 --> 00:21:29.900
BYANG CHUB SEMS KYI SKAL BA CHAD PA YIN

00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:33.780
If you can't recognize

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:36.920
that everybody around
you has been your mom,

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:39.040
then you don't have the SKAL BA

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.667
What's that mean, you guys?
Do you remember, Jigme?

00:21:41.667 --> 00:21:42.500
SKAL BA

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.490
You don't have SKAL BA

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:47.350
CHAD means like RDO RJE GCOD PA

00:21:47.350 --> 00:21:48.200
What's that mean?

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:54.220
You cut the possibility of Buddhahood.

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:58.800
If you can't reach the
state of mind where you see

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:00.507
that everyone has been your mom,

00:22:00.507 --> 00:22:02.820
SKAL BA CHAD means

00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:05.310
you don't have the good
karma to be a Buddha.

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:06.779
You will never be a Buddha.

00:22:06.779 --> 00:22:08.536
SKAL BA CHAD

00:22:08.536 --> 00:22:11.422
That karma seed is cut in you.

00:22:11.422 --> 00:22:12.836
You don't have a choice.

00:22:12.836 --> 00:22:16.477
You have to work on this idea

00:22:16.477 --> 00:22:19.670
that everyone has been your
mom. The most important one.

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:21.883
I love this picture of my mom.

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:27.920
This is me with my mom
and... I don't know.

00:22:28.453 --> 00:22:32.210
I'll tell you, I'm sixty eight years old.

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:36.823
My mom died over forty years ago.

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:43.020
I don't think about her
as much as I used to.

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:45.270
I used to think about her all the time.

00:22:45.270 --> 00:22:47.940
I used to cry all the time.

00:22:47.940 --> 00:22:50.210
Then slowly, as you get
older and older and older,

00:22:50.210 --> 00:22:53.343
and you start... You don't
think about your mom as much.

00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:56.653
But if you do think about your mom,

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:01.820
the point of this
meditation is: let's go back

00:23:01.820 --> 00:23:04.840
to remembering what our mom did for us.

00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:07.010
Let's go back to remembering

00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:10.070
that everyone has been my mother.

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:10.903
He says,

00:23:10.903 --> 00:23:12.927
GZHAN ZAB MO STONG PA NYID SOGS NI

00:23:12.927 --> 00:23:15.710
RIGS PA'I SGO RNAM GRANGS
MANG PO NAS BSAM CHOG PAS

00:23:15.710 --> 00:23:19.060
Look, you can meditate
on emptiness, it's okay.

00:23:19.060 --> 00:23:22.759
You can learn all the
arguments for emptiness.

00:23:22.759 --> 00:23:24.775
Yes, you can spend your time

00:23:24.775 --> 00:23:26.800
RIGS PA'I SGO RNAM GRANGS MANG PO

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:29.730
means you can use logic

00:23:29.730 --> 00:23:33.394
and reasonable thinking to establish

00:23:33.394 --> 00:23:36.746
ZAB MO STONG PA NYID profound emptiness.

00:23:36.746 --> 00:23:38.624
CHOG PA means yes, yes, you can do it.

00:23:38.624 --> 00:23:40.160
CHOG PA means yes, you could

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:42.135
spend your time like that.

00:23:42.135 --> 00:23:44.885
DE TZAM DU RTOGS PAR MI DKA' MOD

00:23:44.885 --> 00:23:49.200
DE TZAM DU RTOGS PAR MI DKA' MOD

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:53.430
Getting to see that
everyone has been your mom

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:55.600
is not as hard as that.

00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:58.747
I admit it's harder to see emptiness.

00:23:58.747 --> 00:24:02.200
DE TZAM DU RTOGS PAR MI DKA' MOD

00:24:02.200 --> 00:24:05.770
That's... I understand

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:07.520
that seeing emptiness is difficult

00:24:07.520 --> 00:24:10.070
and yes, if you tell me,

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:12.480
is bodhichitta easier
or is emptiness easier?

00:24:12.480 --> 00:24:15.208
I got to say maybe
emptiness is very hard. But,

00:24:15.208 --> 00:24:17.802
'DI LA LUNG ZHIG GIS BSAM NA'ANG,

00:24:17.802 --> 00:24:22.802
BSAM PA'I GTING NAS NGES SHES
RNYED PA ZHIG 'BYING DKA' LA

00:24:23.930 --> 00:24:27.500
But I have to say
something about recognizing

00:24:27.500 --> 00:24:31.520
that everyone around you is your mom.

00:24:31.520 --> 00:24:35.890
It's not going to be enough
to just think about it.

00:24:35.890 --> 00:24:38.850
You can't sit there, oh, Geshe-la said

00:24:38.850 --> 00:24:40.707
everyone's been my mom.

00:24:40.707 --> 00:24:44.140
So you're not going to get
to bodhichitta that way.

00:24:44.140 --> 00:24:46.817
It's not enough. He says,

00:24:46.817 --> 00:24:48.967
DBANG RNON CHOS KYI RJES 'BRANG

00:24:48.967 --> 00:24:53.693
Those of you who have a high spiritual IQ,

00:24:54.773 --> 00:24:55.906
RIGS PA

00:24:55.906 --> 00:24:57.122
You're going to have to use,

00:24:57.122 --> 00:24:59.460
you're going to have to think your way

00:24:59.460 --> 00:25:01.940
through this kind of love.

00:25:01.940 --> 00:25:04.230
You're going to have to think your way

00:25:04.230 --> 00:25:05.330
through this kind of love,

00:25:05.330 --> 00:25:07.040
and then you can reach it.

00:25:07.040 --> 00:25:09.970
But you got to learn to think clearly.

00:25:09.970 --> 00:25:13.110
Clear thinking is how you're going

00:25:13.110 --> 00:25:14.540
to reach this kind of love.

00:25:14.540 --> 00:25:16.790
Not by saying, oh, my
mom was so beautiful,

00:25:16.790 --> 00:25:20.140
and I love my mom, and I
feel good about my mom,

00:25:20.140 --> 00:25:24.000
and I wish that my mom was
still alive, that's okay.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:26.660
But if you don't think
your way through it,

00:25:26.660 --> 00:25:29.300
he says, you will never reach bodhichitta.

00:25:29.300 --> 00:25:32.842
You have to think your
way to that kind of love.

00:25:32.842 --> 00:25:34.433
DGOS SHING

00:25:34.433 --> 00:25:35.741
Then he quotes

00:25:35.741 --> 00:25:37.064
RNAM 'GREL

00:25:37.064 --> 00:25:39.730
RNAM 'GREL is a book
by Master Dharmakirti.

00:25:39.730 --> 00:25:42.100
It's called Pramanavarttika.

00:25:42.100 --> 00:25:45.120
It's a commentary on accurate perception.

00:25:45.120 --> 00:25:50.120
It is the mother Buddhist
book about clear thinking,

00:25:50.220 --> 00:25:52.980
how to be... how to think clearly.

00:25:52.980 --> 00:25:55.290
The next picture here,

00:25:55.290 --> 00:25:56.943
you can see

00:25:58.220 --> 00:26:02.000
smoke coming up out of a forest.

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:06.480
This picture is extremely important

00:26:06.480 --> 00:26:07.660
for a Buddhist.

00:26:07.660 --> 00:26:11.000
This picture, if a Buddhist
sees this picture they say,

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:13.370
ah, I know what you're talking about.

00:26:13.370 --> 00:26:15.150
I know what you're talking about.

00:26:15.150 --> 00:26:17.540
Under that smoke there's
definitely a fire.

00:26:17.540 --> 00:26:21.630
In the forest, there's a big, red fire

00:26:21.630 --> 00:26:25.170
behind the green trees,
but we can't see it, right?

00:26:25.170 --> 00:26:26.850
All we can see is the smoke.

00:26:26.850 --> 00:26:29.430
If there's smoke, there's fire.

00:26:29.430 --> 00:26:32.630
If there's smoke, there's fire.

00:26:32.630 --> 00:26:35.260
In this case, in the Lam Rim,

00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:38.270
the fire means everyone you ever met

00:26:38.270 --> 00:26:40.460
in your life was your mom.

00:26:40.460 --> 00:26:42.160
That's the fire.

00:26:42.160 --> 00:26:43.590
What's the smoke?

00:26:43.590 --> 00:26:46.340
We have to look for the smoke.

00:26:46.340 --> 00:26:49.870
We have to look for the proof

00:26:49.870 --> 00:26:52.750
that the people around
me have been my mom.

00:26:52.750 --> 00:26:54.890
We have to try to find the proof.

00:26:54.890 --> 00:26:57.810
The smoke is the proof
that there's a fire.

00:26:57.810 --> 00:27:00.560
Now what's the proof that
everyone has been my mom?

00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:02.350
You know, Geshe-la, give me the proof.

00:27:02.350 --> 00:27:06.820
It's not enough for the
Lama to describe it to you.

00:27:06.820 --> 00:27:08.770
And it's not enough to meditate

00:27:08.770 --> 00:27:10.960
about how much you love your mom.

00:27:10.960 --> 00:27:14.592
You must understand
the reason why everyone

00:27:14.592 --> 00:27:16.730
has definitely been your mom.

00:27:16.730 --> 00:27:18.500
There's no choice.

00:27:18.500 --> 00:27:23.500
You got to use a special kind of thinking

00:27:24.180 --> 00:27:28.270
to prove to yourself beyond the doubt

00:27:28.270 --> 00:27:29.940
that everyone has been your mom.

00:27:29.940 --> 00:27:32.770
And until you go through
that mental exercise,

00:27:32.770 --> 00:27:33.660
it's hopeless.

00:27:33.660 --> 00:27:36.620
You won't be able to get bodhichitta.

00:27:36.620 --> 00:27:38.590
It's never going to happen.

00:27:38.590 --> 00:27:42.830
So now we're going to go on
a big trip in the next class.

00:27:42.830 --> 00:27:44.460
The next class is a long class.

00:27:44.460 --> 00:27:48.890
So get some popcorn before
you start the next class.

00:27:48.890 --> 00:27:50.210
And I'm not going to stop.

00:27:50.210 --> 00:27:51.817
It might take a while.

00:27:51.817 --> 00:27:54.260
But we're going to go.

00:27:54.260 --> 00:27:56.450
He mentions the Dharmakirti.

00:27:56.450 --> 00:27:58.660
And he mentions that Dharmakirti proved

00:27:58.660 --> 00:28:00.360
that everyone has been your mom

00:28:00.360 --> 00:28:02.910
but he doesn't give you the whole proof.

00:28:02.910 --> 00:28:05.240
So guess where we're going to go?

00:28:05.240 --> 00:28:07.210
We're going to go to Dharmakirti

00:28:07.210 --> 00:28:09.110
and we're going to go
through Dharmakirti's proof.

00:28:09.110 --> 00:28:10.450
It's tough.

00:28:10.450 --> 00:28:12.400
And it's delicious.

00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:14.600
So see you in the next class.

00:28:14.600 --> 00:28:17.780
We'll prove that everyone's been your mom.

00:28:17.780 --> 00:28:19.230
See you then.

